# Networkwalks Cybersecurity Internship — Week 02

# Footprinting, Reconnaissance & Network Scanning

## 1. Project Overview

This repository documents the practical activities completed during Week 02 of the Networkwalks Cybersecurity Internship.

The focus of this week was on understanding Footprinting, Reconnaissance, and Network Scanning techniques used in cybersecurity to gather information about a target domain or network.

These activities helped develop practical knowledge of information gathering, DNS enumeration, web technology identification, and network scanning.

## 2. Learning Objectives

The main objectives of this practical work were:

- Understand the fundamentals of Footprinting and Reconnaissance.
- Learn how to collect publicly available information about a domain.
- Identify domain registration and DNS information.
- Explore website technologies and server information.
- Understand DNS enumeration techniques.
- Perform network scanning to identify active hosts and open ports.
- Analyze potential security risks.
- Understand ethical and responsible security testing.

## 3. Practical Modules & Tools Used

The following tools were explored during the practical activities:

| Tool | Purpose |
|---|---|
| WHOIS | Collect domain registration information |
| NSLookup | Identify DNS records and IP addresses |
| WhatWeb | Identify website technologies |
| cURL | Retrieve HTTP response information |
| WAFW00F | Detect Web Application Firewalls |
| DNSRecon | Perform DNS enumeration |
| Nmap | Discover hosts and scan network ports |
| Zenmap | Graphical interface for Nmap |

## 4. Environment & Documentation Stack

**Operating System:** Kali Linux

**Tools:** WHOIS, NSLookup, WhatWeb, cURL, WAFW00F, DNSRecon, Nmap, Zenmap

**Documentation:** GitHub README, screenshots, and practical findings

**Testing Environment:** Authorized lab environment and permitted targets only.

